{"title":"Common internal tangent line","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>common internal <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tangent\" title=\"Tangent\">tangent</a></b> of two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circles</a> is a tangent of both circles that intersects the segment joining the centers of two circles.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Common_internal_tangent_line&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introductory\">Introductory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Common_internal_tangent_line&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Introductory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">Circles</a> with <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Center\" title=\"Center\">centers</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> have <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radius\" title=\"Radius\">radii</a> 3 and 8, respectively. A <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\"> common internal tangent</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Intersect\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Intersect\">intersects</a> the circles at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line\" title=\"Line\">Lines</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/8/5c884057c1218625814fc38808eb0f395aac6928.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=5$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />? <div style=\"text-align:right;\">(<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">2006 AMC 12A, #16</a>)</div></li></ul>\n<figure typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2006_AMC12A-16.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/0a/2006_AMC12A-16.png/200px-2006_AMC12A-16.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/0a/2006_AMC12A-16.png/300px-2006_AMC12A-16.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/0a/2006_AMC12A-16.png/400px-2006_AMC12A-16.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><br />\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Common_internal_tangent_line&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018080844\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.027 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 42/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 325/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1517/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.511      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.511      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5322:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018080844 and revision id 223203. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}